Milestone 4 packaged Windows isolation

Reason
The normal NSIS product identity, hooks, uninstall registry entry and asynchronous uninstall semantics can mutate or race a real Beaver installation. The packaged E2E journey must own a distinct product and profile from build through removal.

Changes
- Add a Windows-only E2E bundle overlay named Beaver E2E with identifier com.clgo.dash.e2e and no production installer hooks.
- Pass NSIS /D= and _?= arguments verbatim and last so paths containing spaces stay inside the isolated profile and cleanup waits for the real uninstaller.
- Attempt bounded cleanup after partial installation failures and normalize preparation errors.
- Limit packaged mode to Windows. macOS keeps the existing native .app journey because the normal runner already launches the bundle binary.
- Tighten CI assertions so the Linux job cannot match test:e2e:packaged accidentally.

Verification observed
- node --test scripts/e2e/packaged-app.test.mjs scripts/e2e/e2e-process.test.mjs: 27 passed, 0 failed.
- git diff --check: passed.

Limits
The NSIS install/uninstall flow is not executable on macOS. Windows native proof and cross-OS CI are required before merge.

Rectification apres re-review (2026-08-18): l'assertion CI resserree par ce commit concernait Windows et macOS, pas Linux. Le resserrement Linux exact est apporte plus tard par 480141dd.

